# jsonData is ~98MB of one-time Climax migration data, but it is NOT all
# orphaned - which is what the previous blanket "jsonData" rule assumed, and
# why the frontend image could not build at all: eight live components import
# ports.json (BL print, job list, delivery order, voyage, invoice print) and
# two import airports.json.
#
# So exclude the large files nothing imports, and keep the ~6MB that the build
# genuinely needs.
jsonData/destinations.json
jsonData/destinationDetails.json
jsonData/destinationDetailTwo.json
jsonData/Vouchers.json
jsonData/invoices.json
jsonData/Invocies.json

# Seanet's own historical job records (SNS_SEJ, SNS_AE, ...). Every import of
# these in BackupModal.js is commented out, so nothing needs them - and they
# are one customer's operational data, which must never end up in an image
# shipped to another.

# One-time migration seeds - real invoice records, must not enter an image.
seeds
# NOTE: .env is intentionally NOT ignored — the build reads it for the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* backend URLs (public config, no secrets).
jsonData/oldJobs
